&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Engineering Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;At Okta, our motto is &quot;Always On&quot;&amp;nbsp; and nowhere do we embrace that more than in Technical Operations. We strive to build the most reliable and performant systems on the planet through the skillful use of automation. If you like to be challenged and have a passion for solving large-scale automation, testing, and tuning problems, we would love to hear from you. The ideal candidate is someone who exemplifies the ethics of, “If you have to do something more than once, automate it” and who can rapidly self-educate on new concepts and tools.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Multi-Cloud Migrations:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct the migration of legacy and containerized services to scalable Kubernetes clusters across &lt;strong&gt;AWS (EKS) and GCP (GKE)&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring high availability and seamless traffic management between providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect Hybrid Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and optimize resilient Kubernetes architectures that leverage cloud-native features from both AWS and GCP to meet global business demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified CI/CD &amp;amp; GitOps:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain cross-cloud pipelines using Spinnaker, ArgoCD, or GitLab CI, automating deployments to both EKS and GKE clusters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC):&lt;/strong&gt; Use Terraform to provision and manage complex infrastructure across multiple providers, maintaining a single source of truth for cloud resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Enhance multi-cloud monitoring using Prometheus, Grafana, and the ELK Stack, creating unified dashboards that aggregate metrics from CloudWatch and Google Cloud Monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Cloud Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement and enforce security best practices including cross-cloud IAM roles, Workload Identity, and Service Mesh (Istio/Anthos Service Mesh) for secure pod-to-pod communication across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Response:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in on-call rotations, performing root cause analysis for production issues across a diverse, multi-cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring to the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;k8s Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Expert knowledge of core Kubernetes (Pods, StatefulSets, PV/PVC) with hands-on experience managing both Amazon EKS and Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in Docker and advanced deployment patterns using Helm, Kustomize, and Kubernetes Operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud-Native Networking:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of VPC peering, Interconnect/Direct Connect, Ingress Controllers, and Service Meshes (Istio, Linkerd) for secure multi-cloud microservices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Expert-level Terraform skills specifically for multi-provider environments (AWS and GCP modules).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global CI/CD:&lt;/strong&gt; Extensive experience with GitOps (ArgoCD) and deployment tools that support multi-cluster targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Logging:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience setting up centralized observability platforms that integrate with Fluentd, Prometheus, and Google Cloud Operations suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with RBAC, Network Policies, and Workload Identity. Experience with secrets management using HashiCorp Vault or native Cloud Secret Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years migrating and architecting mission-critical workloads in multi-cloud environments (AWS &amp;amp; GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on experience with the AWS ecosystem (EC2, S3, RDS) and GCP ecosystem (Compute Engine, Cloud Storage, BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience using Terraform to manage infrastructure at scale across multiple cloud providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in Go or Python for building custom automation and cloud integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred Certifications: CKA/CKAD, AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, or Google Professional Cloud DevOps Engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;br&gt;#P24494_3575673&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
